.helper`. Then rebuild `childEnv` from `CHILD_ENV_NAMES` (`PATH`, `HOME`, `USER`, `LOGNAME`, `SHELL`, `TMPDIR`, `TMP`, `TEMP`, `LANG`, `TERM`, `TERM_PROGRAM`, `COLORTERM` and `NO_COLOR`) and `CHILD_ENV_PREFIXES` (`LC_`, `XDG_`, `ANTHROPIC_`, `CLAUDE_`, `CODEX_`, `OPENAI_`, `OPENCODE_`, `LLMGATEWAY_`, `PI_`, `DEVIN_`, `DSH_`, `DEEPSEEK_`, `OLLAMA_`, `SPECKIT_`, `SKILL_ADVISOR_`, `SYSTEM_SPEC_GATE_` and `MK_`), then set the GitHub and git overrides as today. Delete `GITHUB_TOKEN_VARS` and rewrite the comment above it to say a turn runs with bypassed permissions, so it gets only what a runtime needs to start and authenticate, and every other credential in the operator's shell stays out. Verify: before the change the case fails on `SSH_AUTH_SOCK`, after it `VX tests/command-behaviour-guards.vitest.ts` reports 0 failed and `node --check $R` exits 0.\n108: - [x] T022 Refuse a live arm outside a marked arena (`R`, `BG`). Test first: in `BG`, add a case on a temporary folder after `git init -q`: `liveArmRefusal(dir)` returns code `arena_unprepared`, after writing `<dir>/.git/MARK` it returns `null` and after `git remote add origin https://example.invalid/x.git` it returns code `remote_present` with `remotes` `['origin']`. Then export `liveArmRefusal(root)`: it runs `git -C <root> -c core.fsmonitor=false remote` and returns the `remote_present` refusal when a name is listed, else resolves the output of `git -C <root> rev-parse --git-path MARK` against `root` and returns `{ ok: false, code: 'arena_unprepared', marker: <that path> }` when the file is missing, else `null`. In `runTurn`'s first-turn block, call it on `REPO_ROOT` in place of the `remoteNames()` check, still only when the run is not a dry run. Remove `remoteNames` when nothing else calls it. Add a comment saying a remote is the one way a turn reaches outside, and the marker proves the checkout came from the arena builder. Verify: before the change the import is `undefined` and the case fails, after it `VX tests/co